WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.010
A cloud landing zone is a starting point. Your mission still

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.370
needs a path it can execute and sustain. Cloud Waypoint helps

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.730
you move from cloud decision to durable operation, with useful work

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.316
your agency can own.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:21.284
Start where you are: choosing a path, establishing the foundation, preparing

00:00:21.284 --> 00:00:25.752
a first workload, or improving operations. Together, we define the outcome,

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:29.408
scope, decision owners, and handover for a bounded engagement.

00:00:30.908 --> 00:00:35.711
We draw on the NIST Risk Management Framework, security controls, the

00:00:35.711 --> 00:00:40.514
DoD Cloud Computing Security Requirements Guide, and Zero Trust. Operating practices

00:00:40.514 --> 00:00:45.316
add reliability and cost discipline. These guide the questions; your evidence

00:00:45.316 --> 00:00:46.626
shapes the answer.

00:00:48.126 --> 00:00:52.700
Here is the actual Studio, using a fictional engagement. Intake records

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.274
the mission, scope, operating context, people, and handling rules. Evidence stays

00:00:57.274 --> 00:01:01.847
linked to its source, owner, and limitations, so the recommendation can

00:01:01.847 --> 00:01:03.511
be explained and challenged.

00:01:05.011 --> 00:01:08.650
Your team is an active partner. Respond to data calls, bring

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.289
procedures and evidence through approved channels, and make owners available for

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:15.929
interviews and workshops. Confirm facts and resolve disagreements. Missing information stays

00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:16.260
visible.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.974
What do you take away? This complete example groups fifteen outputs

00:01:21.974 --> 00:01:26.188
into five connected packages, plus an implementation handoff. Depth follows the

00:01:26.188 --> 00:01:30.019
agreed scope, with evidence, open work, and next owners visible.

00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:35.987
The foundations receipt establishes the engagement basis. The assessment and technical

00:01:35.987 --> 00:01:40.456
analysis explain the current position and supporting evidence. The executive brief

00:01:40.456 --> 00:01:44.924
brings the material findings, choices, uncertainties, and recommended next decisions into

00:01:44.924 --> 00:01:46.956
a form leadership can use.

00:01:48.456 --> 00:01:52.577
The transformation storyboard connects the story. The road ahead and transformation

00:01:52.577 --> 00:01:56.699
plan turn it into proposed work, dependencies, owners, and acceptance measures.

00:01:56.699 --> 00:02:00.821
Your team reviews the priorities and sequence, so the plan reflects

00:02:00.821 --> 00:02:03.069
a decision you can act on.

00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:08.908
For the agreed GSS scope, the concept of operations describes how

00:02:08.908 --> 00:02:13.247
the environment is intended to work. The draft system security plan

00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:17.587
and plan of action and milestones organize control responsibilities, evidence needs,

00:02:17.587 --> 00:02:19.954
and unresolved work for accountable review.

00:02:21.454 --> 00:02:25.797
The authorization readiness receipt, GSS exit receipt, and readiness report preserve

00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:30.140
the conditions and evidence behind the next gate. They support preparation

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.484
and review. Authorization and risk acceptance remain with your responsible officials.

00:02:35.984 --> 00:02:40.865
The delivery note and closeout receipt inventory the handover. The implementation

00:02:40.865 --> 00:02:45.746
handoff carries boundaries, dependencies, responsibilities, and acceptance criteria to your chosen

00:02:45.746 --> 00:02:50.627
team. The continuation view keeps weekly changes, open actions, and client

00:02:50.627 --> 00:02:51.514
inputs visible.

00:02:53.014 --> 00:02:57.344
Success takes participation: timely evidence, candid interviews, review of the work,

00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:01.674
named owners, and knowledge transfer. The result is a defensible path,

00:03:01.674 --> 00:03:06.004
useful artifacts, and a next move your team understands. If you

00:03:06.004 --> 00:03:09.940
cannot run it after we leave, it does not ship.
